title: consent.exe Execution from Unusual Location
status: experimental
description: Detects execution of consent.exe from outside its legitimate system directory. Attackers copy the signed consent.exe next to a malicious msimg32.dll to perform DLL side-loading, as seen in the BumbleBee loader.
references:
    - https://thedfirreport.com/2026/06/29/from-bing-search-to-ransomware-bumblebee-and-adaptixc2-deliver-akira-3/
author: Sümeyra Yüksel
date: 2026/10/20
tags:
    - attack.defense-evasion
    - attack.t1574.001
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
    service: sysmon
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith: '\consent.exe'
    filter_legit_path:
        Image|startswith:
            - 'C:\Windows\System32\'
            - 'C:\Windows\SysWOW64\'
    condition: selection and not filter_legit_path
fields:
    - Image
    - ParentImage
    - User
falsepositives:
    - consent.exe is a signed Windows binary that normally runs only from System32
level: high
